stasis or other pathological changes. Additionally, the liver can be influenced by factors such as obesity and nutrition, with its size potentially decreasing significantly with very low-calorie diets prior to surgery.\n\nAs a nutrient-rich organ meat, hígado provides significant amounts of vitamins and minerals, including iron, and is known to elevate uric acid levels when consumed due to its purine content. Overall, the hígado is an essential organ that plays a multifaceted role in maintaining metabolic homeostasis and overall health.\",37\r\n4912,FOSFOLÍPIDOS,\"FOSFOLÍPIDOS, or phospholipids, are a class of lipids that serve as a major component of all cell membranes, playing a crucial role in maintaining cellular structure and function. They are essential for various cellular processes, including those that require copper for their synthesis. Additionally, phospholipids are included in some nutritional products, highlighting their importance not only in cellular biology but also in nutrition.\",3\r\n2244,ACIDOSIS LACTICA,\"Acidosis láctica, or lactic acidosis, is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lactic acid in the body, which can occur due to various metabolic disturbances. This condition is particularly relevant in patients with Glycogen Storage Disease I (GSDI), where abnormal glucose metabolism can lead to increased lactate levels in the blood. The buildup of lactic acid is often associated with inadequate oxygen supply to tissues, which exacerbates the condition. \n\nIn addition to GSDI, lactic acidosis can also arise from other metabolic derangements, such as fructose-1,6-bisphosphate deficiency. Furthermore, it can be worsened by the fermentation of unabsorbed carbohydrates in the colon, contributing to malabsorption issues. However, there are potential interventions, such as medium-chain triglyceride (MCT) supplementation, that may help improve the condition. Overall, acidosis láctica is a complex clinical manifestation that requires careful management, especially in individuals with specific metabolic disorders.\",8\r\n9432,GLUCOSA-6-FOSFATASA,\"Glucosa-6-fosfatasa is an essential enzyme involved in glucose metabolism. It plays a critical role in converting glucose-6-phosphate into glucose, facilitating the release of free glucose into the bloodstream. This enzymatic activity is vital for maintaining normal blood glucose levels. A deficiency in glucosa-6-fosfatasa is central to the diagnosis of glucogenosis de tipo I, also known as enfermedad de Von Gierke, a genetic disorder characterized by impaired glucose production and storage.\",4\r\n11805,CUPROENZIMAS,\"CUPROENZIMAS refers to enzymes that contain copper and are essential for various biochemical processes in the body. These processes include electron transport and neurotransmitter metabolism, highlighting the critical role that copper-containing enzymes play in maintaining physiological functions.\",11\r\n10717,GLUCOGENOSIS DE TIPO I,\"Glucogenosis de tipo I is a metabolic disorder characterized by the deficiency of the enzyme glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to hypoglycemia and lactic acidosis.\",7\r\n10718,ENFERMEDAD DE VON GIERKE,\"Enfermedad de Von Gierke is a condition marked by the deficiency of glucose-6-phosphatase, resulting in the accumulation of glycogen in the liver and associated metabolic issues.\",4\r\n10733,VON GIERKE TYPE IA,\"Von Gierke Type Ia is a specific type of hepatic glycogen storage disease characterized by a deficiency in glucose-6-phosphatase, leading to severe hypoglycemia and other metabolic complications.\",3\r\n11811,SUPERÓXIDO DISMUTASA,\"Superóxido dismutasa is a copper-containing enzyme that plays a crucial role in protecting cells from oxidative damage. It catalyzes the conversion of superoxide radicals, which are harmful byproducts of cellular metabolism, into oxygen and hydrogen peroxide. By facilitating this conversion, superóxido dismutasa helps to mitigate the effects of oxidative stress, thereby safeguarding cellular integrity and function.\",2\r\n15294,C-REACTIVA PROTEÍNA,,1\r\n11819,METALOTIONEINAS,\"Metallothioneins are proteins that bind heavy metals, including copper, and play a role in metal metabolism and detoxification.\",1\r\n6565,CITOCROMO C OXIDASA,\"Citocromo C oxidasa is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the electron transport chain, which is essential for cellular respiration. This enzyme is particularly noted for its increased activity in patients with MELAS (Mitochondrial Encephalomyopathy, Lactic Acidosis, and Stroke-like episodes), a condition that can impact the availability of nitric oxide in the body.\",2\r\n11807,TEJIDO ELÁSTICO,Elastic tissue is a type of connective tissue that requires copper for its synthesis and maintenance.,1\r\n11812,NEUROTRANSMISORES,Neurotransmitters are chemical messengers in the nervous system that are influenced by copper-containing enzymes in their metabolism.,1\r\n8332,HUESOS,\"HUESOS, or bones, are essential structures in the body that play a crucial role in providing support and protection to various organs. They are dependent on copper for their development and maintenance, highlighting the importance of this mineral in bone health. Additionally, certain types of bones can pose a choking hazard for patients with dysphagia, a condition that affects swallowing. This dual aspect of bones emphasizes their significance in both physiological functions and potential health risks.\",1\r\n10719,BIOQUÍMICO,Bioquímico refers to the biochemical analysis performed to diagnose conditions like glucogenosis de tipo I and enfermedad de Von Gierke.,2\r\n9427,GLUCOSA-6-FOSFATO,\"GLUCOSA-6-FOSFATO es un metabolito clave en el metabolismo de la glucosa y la galactosa. Se trata de una forma fosforilada de la glucosa que desempeña un papel fundamental en la glucólisis y el metabolismo del glucógeno. Además, la glucosa-6-fosfato actúa como un intermediario en el metabolismo de la glucosa y es crucial en el proceso de gluc